{"title":"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are externally tangent to each other and internally tangent to a larger circle. What is the radius of the large circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfe6128d93d11ca58bb6fb5b947d91d747001c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{6}}{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac{2 + 3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{3 + 2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"561\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The situation is shown in the picture below. The radius we seek is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7543c4e22ef5e113ce982fee2f419153d717a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SD = AD + AS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd842e36ed64086a882c190267900ce65d1f7017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f861cdd52e65580668061b0eaf3c023960029f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS$\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38bd36e353df831303c0de895a9ec614cf3e7202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> of the altitude of this triangle. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94da2629f2bab6c8568172b863637c792608ef72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS = \\frac23 \\cdot \\sqrt 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore the radius we seek is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c0e1ffca5584f4d2588cfbe65bc33de4b444ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + \\frac23 \\cdot \\sqrt 3 = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)\\ }\\frac{3+2\\sqrt{3}}3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"220\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/056b92c537632c2d904effcbd77cab0e9d61be72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(2cm); pair A=(0,0), B=dir(0)*2, C=dir(60)*2; draw(circle(A,1)); draw(circle(B,1)); draw(circle(C,1)); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); draw(A--B--C--cycle);  pair D=A+dir(210), E=B+dir(-30), F=C+dir(90); draw(circumcircle(D,E,F)); dot(D); dot(E); dot(F);  pair S=(A+B+C)/3; dot(S);  draw(S--D); draw(S--E); draw(S--F);  label(&quot;$S$&quot;,S,S); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,ENE); [/asy]\" width=\"408\" height=\"412\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes%27_Circle_Formula\" title=\"Descartes&#39; Circle Formula\">Descartes' Circle Formula</a>, we can assign curvatures to all the circles: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5028215beac6db9339110bb79ff23669544430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"37\" /> (b/c the bigger circle is externally tangent to all the other circles, the radius of the bigger circle is negative). Then, we can solve:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec8242e8275295d108dc91d0fa76eb026c5b38b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(1^2+1^2+1^2+(-\\frac{1}{r})^2) = (1+1+1-\\frac{1}{r})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"339\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a446b043698ca0bde483f403172768acadfcf0f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)\\ }\\frac{3+2\\sqrt{3}}3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"148\" height=\"54\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B\">2004 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-i